<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures rise, further gains seen.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures rise, further gains seen.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney Futures Exchange wheat futures traded higher on Friday following Chicago's rise as local brokers began to talk of a potential significant upturn.</p>
<p>January 1998 rose by A$2.00 to A$165.00 in two lots traded.</p>
<p>Settlement prices for the more distant contracts generally rose by about A$5.00 a tonne while settlements for near-term contracts remained generally steady.</p>
<p>Gary Booth of Ord Minnett Jardine Fleming Futures Ltd said that despite Australia's record wheat crop most wheat was already committed.  </p>
